WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.780
Tō Tātou Takiwā, Tō Tātou Wāheke 2048.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.460
Te Rautaki Whanake Takiwā

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.040
The Waimakariri District is a great place

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.000
to live, work, visit and play.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.660
And this has not gone unnoticed, our population
and business sectors have been growing rapidly.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.520
About 57,000 people currently call the Waimakariri
District their home

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:36.100
and by 2048 our population may be close to 100,000 people.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.740
We are now planning on how best to manage
that growth over the next 30 years.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.740
Where will people live, work and play?

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:50.059
Do we have enough land for business and housing
and what should happen in our rural areas?

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.620
How will our infrastructure meet this increased
demand

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.300
and how should we safeguard our natural environment?

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.000
The District Development Strategy will guide
long term growth in our district and provide

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.730
the direction for more detailed Council documents
such as the upcoming District Plan review.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.860
It covers seven main themes, which we’ll
be taking a closer look at in later videos:

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:18.840
We’d like your feedback on this draft strategy
before it’s finalised later this year.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:28.960
You can view the document at any Council Service
Centre or visit waimakariri.govt.nz/districtdevelopment

